# SPEC: §9, §16
# COVERS: kind:handle set
# ERROR_KIND: handle
# ERROR: no editor
# EXIT: 1
# Amendment A2 added "handle" for an editor object a script cannot
# resolve.  `set({})` from a headless run is the shape fuzz_fl_vm hit
# (seed 20261003): a well-typed call with no editor to apply it to.  It
# raises the documented kind, catchably, rather than some kind outside
# §9.1's thirteen -- and uncaught it exits 1.
import io
try {
    set({})
} catch e {
    # OUT: handle
    io.print(e.kind)
}
set({})
